	field - select fields or columns from a fileSyntax		field -s=c [ n ] .....Description	The field command copies specified whitespace separated fields from	the standard input to the standard output. Fields are numbered from	1 and a field may be requested more than once. Output fields are	tab separated.	If the -s option is present the separator is a single instance of 	the given character.Source	The original version of this program was published in 'The UNIX	System V Environment' by Stephen R Bourne, 1987. This was a basic	form of the program. Martin Gregorie ported it to OS9/68K, adding	options and error traps. The program limits documented below were	present in the original; they are sufficiently large that it was	not considered worth while re-implementing the program to remove	them.Bugs	The number of input or output fields may not exceed 256 and the 	maximum line length is 4096 characters.Author	Martin Gregorie	10 Sadlers Mead	Harlow	Essex	CM18 6HG	Gregorie@LFGMS.logica.com